{"id":"mahabharata-3-011","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":11,"title":"एकादशोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 11 · Maitreya curses Duryodhana","summary":{"en":"The sage Maitreya, having met the Pandavas in the forest, comes to court and urges Duryodhana to make peace. When Duryodhana scornfully slaps his thigh, Maitreya curses him that Bhima will break that thigh in battle, and departs as Vidura tells of the slaying of Kirmira.","kn":"ಕಾಡಿನಲ್ಲಿ ಪಾಂಡವರನ್ನು ಭೇಟಿಯಾದ ಮೈತ್ರೇಯ ಋಷಿ ಆಸ್ಥಾನಕ್ಕೆ ಬಂದು ಸಂಧಿ ಮಾಡಿಕೋ ಎಂದು ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನಿಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾರೆ. ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನು ತಿರಸ್ಕಾರದಿಂದ ತೊಡೆ ತಟ್ಟಿದಾಗ ಯುದ್ಧದಲ್ಲಿ ಭೀಮನು ಆ ತೊಡೆ ಮುರಿಯಲೆಂದು ಶಪಿಸಿ ಹೊರಡುತ್ತಾರೆ; ವಿದುರನು ಕಿರ್ಮೀರವಧೆಯ ಕಥೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"वन में पाण्डवों से मिलकर ऋषि मैत्रेय दरबार में आते हैं और दुर्योधन से सन्धि करने का आग्रह करते हैं। जब दुर्योधन तिरस्कार से अपनी जाँघ ठोकता है, मैत्रेय शाप देते हैं कि युद्ध में भीम वह जाँघ तोड़ेंगे, और चले जाते हैं, जबकि विदुर किर्मीर-वध की बात बताते हैं।","te":"అడవిలో పాండవులను కలిసిన మైత్రేయ ఋషి ఆస్థానానికి వచ్చి సంధి చేసుకోమని దుర్యోధనునికి చెబుతాడు. దుర్యోధనుడు తిరస్కారంతో తొడ చరచగా యుద్ధంలో భీముడు ఆ తొడను విరుస్తాడని శపించి వెళ్తాడు; విదురుడు కిర్మీర వధ గురించి చెబుతాడు.","ta":"காட்டில் பாண்டவர்களைச் சந்தித்த மைத்ரேய முனிவர் அரசவைக்கு வந்து சமாதானம் செய்யுமாறு துரியோதனனை வேண்டுகிறார். துரியோதனன் ஏளனமாகத் தொடையைத் தட்ட, போரில் பீமன் அந்தத் தொடையை முறிப்பான் என்று சபித்துச் செல்கிறார்; விதுரர் கிர்மீர வதம் பற்றிச் சொல்கிறார்.","ml":"കാട്ടിൽ പാണ്ഡവരെ കണ്ട മൈത്രേയൻ സഭയിലെത്തി ദുര്യോധനനോട് സന്ധിക്ക് അപേക്ഷിക്കുന്നു. പരിഹാസത്തോടെ ദുര്യോധനൻ തുടയിൽ തട്ടുമ്പോൾ, യുദ്ധത്തിൽ ഭീമൻ ആ തുട തകർക്കുമെന്ന് മൈത്രേയൻ ശപിക്കുന്നു; വിദുരൻ കിർമ്മീരവധത്തെക്കുറിച്ച് പറയുമ്പോൾ അദ്ദേഹം പോകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.11; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"आरण्यकपर्व","titleEn":"Aranyaka Parva (Into the forest)","verses":[{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"एवमेतन्महाप्राज्ञ यथा वदसि नो मुने ।\nअहं चैव विजानामि सर्वे चेमे नराधिपाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great sage, it is just as you say; I know it, and so do all these kings."}},{"n":2,"text":"भवांस्तु मन्यते साधु यत्कुरूणां सुखोदयम् ।\nतदेव विदुरोऽप्याह भीष्मो द्रोणश्च मां मुने ॥","meaning":{"en":"What you think good, that brings happiness to the Kurus, sage, is just what Vidura, Bhishma and Drona also tell me."}},{"n":3,"text":"यदि त्वहमनुग्राह्यः कौरवेषु दया यदि ।\nअनुशाधि दुरात्मानं पुत्रं दुर्योधनं मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"If I deserve your favor, and if you have compassion for the Kauravas, instruct my wicked-souled son Duryodhana."}},{"text":"व्यास उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vyasa said:"}},{"n":4,"text":"अयमायाति वै राजन्मैत्रेयो भगवानृषिः ।\nअन्वीय पाण्डवान्भ्रातॄनिहैवास्मद्दिदृक्षया ॥","meaning":{"en":"The revered sage Maitreya is coming here, king, after visiting the Pandava brothers, wishing to see us."}},{"n":5,"text":"एष दुर्योधनं पुत्रं तव राजन्महानृषिः ।\nअनुशास्ता यथान्यायं शमायास्य कुलस्य ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"This great sage will instruct your son Duryodhana, king, as is proper, for the peace of your family."}},{"n":6,"text":"ब्रूयाद्यदेष राजेन्द्र तत्कार्यमविशङ्कया ।\nअक्रियायां हि कार्यस्य पुत्रं ते शप्स्यते रुषा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Do without hesitation what he says, lord of kings; if it is not done, he will curse your son in anger."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":7,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा ययौ व्यासो मैत्रेयः प्रत्यदृश्यत ।\nपूजया प्रतिजग्राह सपुत्रस्तं नराधिपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So saying, Vyasa left, and Maitreya came into view. The king and his son received him with honor."}},{"n":8,"text":"दत्त्वार्घ्याद्याः क्रियाः सर्वा विश्रान्तं मुनिपुंगवम् ।\nप्रश्रयेणाब्रवीद्राजा धृतराष्ट्रोऽम्बिकासुतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"After offering the water of welcome and all the rites, once the best of sages had rested, King Dhritarashtra, Ambika's son, said to him with humility."}},{"n":9,"text":"सुखेनागमनं कच्चिद्भगवन्कुरुजाङ्गले ।\nकच्चित्कुशलिनो वीरा भ्रातरः पञ्च पाण्डवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Venerable one, was your journey to the Kuru land pleasant? Are the five Pandava brother heroes well?"}},{"n":10,"text":"समये स्थातुमिच्छन्ति कच्चिच्च पुरुषर्षभाः ।\nकच्चित्कुरूणां सौभ्रात्रमव्युच्छिन्नं भविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Do those bulls among men wish to abide by their agreement? Will the brotherhood of the Kurus remain unbroken?"}},{"text":"मैत्रेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Maitreya said:"}},{"n":11,"text":"तीर्थयात्रामनुक्रामन्प्राप्तोऽस्मि कुरुजाङ्गलम् ।\nयदृच्छया धर्मराजं दृष्टवान्काम्यके वने ॥","meaning":{"en":"Making a pilgrimage, I reached the Kuru land, and by chance I saw Dharmaraja in the Kamyaka forest."}},{"n":12,"text":"तं जटाजिनसंवीतं तपोवननिवासिनम् ।\nसमाजग्मुर्महात्मानं द्रष्टुं मुनिगणाः प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"Clad in matted hair and deerskin, living in the forest hermitage, he was visited, lord, by hosts of sages come to see that great soul."}},{"n":13,"text":"तत्राश्रौषं महाराज पुत्राणां तव विभ्रमम् ।\nअनयं द्यूतरूपेण महापायमुपस्थितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There, great king, I heard of the folly of your sons, the great calamity that came through the dice game."}},{"n":14,"text":"ततोऽहं त्वामनुप्राप्तः कौरवाणामवेक्षया ।\nसदा ह्यभ्यधिकः स्नेहः प्रीतिश्च त्वयि मे प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then I came to you out of concern for the Kauravas, for I always have great affection and fondness for you, lord."}},{"n":15,"text":"नैतदौपयिकं राजंस्त्वयि भीष्मे च जीवति ।\nयदन्योन्येन ते पुत्रा विरुध्यन्ते नराधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"It is not fitting, king, while you and Bhishma live, that your sons should be at odds with one another."}},{"n":16,"text":"मेढीभूतः स्वयं राजन्निग्रहे प्रग्रहे भवान् ।\nकिमर्थमनयं घोरमुत्पतन्तमुपेक्षसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"You yourself are the bull, king, in controlling and holding back; why do you ignore the terrible mischief that is rising?"}},{"n":17,"text":"दस्यूनामिव यद्वृत्तं सभायां कुरुनन्दन ।\nतेन न भ्राजसे राजंस्तापसानां समागमे ॥","meaning":{"en":"By what happened in the assembly, Kuru's delight, conduct like that of robbers, you do not shine in a gathering of ascetics."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":18,"text":"ततो व्यावृत्य राजानं दुर्योधनममर्षणम् ।\nउवाच श्लक्ष्णया वाचा मैत्रेयो भगवानृषिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the revered sage Maitreya turned to the king's angry son Duryodhana and spoke in gentle words."}},{"n":19,"text":"दुर्योधन महाबाहो निबोध वदतां वर ।\nवचनं मे महाप्राज्ञ ब्रुवतो यद्धितं तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana, mighty-armed, best of speakers, wise one, hear my words, which I speak for your good."}},{"n":20,"text":"मा द्रुहः पाण्डवान्राजन्कुरुष्व हितमात्मनः ।\nपाण्डवानां कुरूणां च लोकस्य च नरर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Do not harm the Pandavas, king; do what is good for yourself, bull among men, and for the Pandavas, the Kurus and the world."}},{"n":21,"text":"ते हि सर्वे नरव्याघ्राः शूरा विक्रान्तयोधिनः ।\nसर्वे नागायुतप्राणा वज्रसंहनना दृढाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They are all tigers among men, brave and valiant fighters, each with the strength of ten thousand elephants, firm, with bodies hard as thunderbolts."}},{"n":22,"text":"सत्यव्रतपराः सर्वे सर्वे पुरुषमानिनः ।\nहन्तारो देवशत्रूणां रक्षसां कामरूपिणाम् ।\nहिडिम्बबकमुख्यानां किर्मीरस्य च रक्षसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"All keep to vows of truth, all are proud of their manhood. They are slayers of the gods' enemies and of shape-changing demons, among them Hidimba, Baka and others, and the demon Kirmira."}},{"n":23,"text":"इतः प्रच्यवतां रात्रौ यः स तेषां महात्मनाम् ।\nआवृत्य मार्गं रौद्रात्मा तस्थौ गिरिरिवाचलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Leaving this place by night, that cruel-souled Kirmira stood blocking their path like an unmoving mountain."}},{"n":24,"text":"तं भीमः समरश्लाघी बलेन बलिनां वरः ।\nजघान पशुमारेण व्याघ्रः क्षुद्रमृगं यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhima, who delights in battle, best of the strong in strength, killed him as one kills a sacrificial animal, as a tiger kills a small deer."}},{"n":25,"text":"पश्य दिग्विजये राजन्यथा भीमेन पातितः ।\nजरासंधो महेष्वासो नागायुतबलो युधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Look, king, how in the conquest of the quarters Bhima felled Jarasandha, the great archer with the strength of ten thousand elephants, in battle."}},{"n":26,"text":"संबन्धी वासुदेवश्च येषां श्यालश्च पार्षतः ।\nकस्तान्युधि समासीत जरामरणवान्नरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vasudeva Krishna is their relative, and Prishata's son Dhrishtadyumna is their brother-in-law. What mortal subject to old age and death could face them in battle?"}},{"n":27,"text":"तस्य ते शम एवास्तु पाण्डवैर्भरतर्षभ ।\nकुरु मे वचनं राजन्मा मृत्युवशमन्वगाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let there be peace with the Pandavas for you, bull of the Bharatas. Heed my words, king; do not fall under the sway of death."}},{"n":28,"text":"एवं तु ब्रुवतस्तस्य मैत्रेयस्य विशां पते ।\nऊरुं गजकराकारं करेणाभिजघान सः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Maitreya spoke so, lord of men, Duryodhana slapped his own thigh, which was like an elephant's trunk, with his hand."}},{"n":29,"text":"दुर्योधनः स्मितं कृत्वा चरणेनालिखन्महीम् ।\nन किंचिदुक्त्वा दुर्मेधास्तस्थौ किंचिदवाङ्मुखः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Smiling, Duryodhana scratched the ground with his foot and, dull-witted, stood saying nothing, with his face slightly lowered."}},{"n":30,"text":"तमशुश्रूषमाणं तु विलिखन्तं वसुंधराम् ।\nदृष्ट्वा दुर्योधनं राजन्मैत्रेयं कोप आविशत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Duryodhana not listening and scratching the earth, anger entered Maitreya, king."}},{"n":31,"text":"स कोपवशमापन्नो मैत्रेयो मुनिसत्तमः ।\nविधिना संप्रयुक्तश्च शापायास्य मनो दधे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Overcome by anger, the best of sages, urged on by fate, set his mind on cursing him."}},{"n":32,"text":"ततः स वार्युपस्पृश्य कोपसंरक्तलोचनः ।\nमैत्रेयो धार्तराष्ट्रं तमशपद्दुष्टचेतसम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, touching water, his eyes red with rage, Maitreya cursed that evil-minded son of Dhritarashtra."}},{"n":33,"text":"यस्मात्त्वं मामनादृत्य नेमां वाचं चिकीर्षसि ।\nतस्मादस्याभिमानस्य सद्यः फलमवाप्नुहि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Since you disregard me and will not heed my words, receive at once the fruit of this pride."}},{"n":34,"text":"त्वदभिद्रोहसंयुक्तं युद्धमुत्पत्स्यते महत् ।\nयत्र भीमो गदापातैस्तवोरुं भेत्स्यते बली ॥","meaning":{"en":"A great war born of hostility to you will arise, in which mighty Bhima will smash your thigh with blows of his mace."}},{"n":35,"text":"इत्येवमुक्ते वचने धृतराष्ट्रो महीपतिः ।\nप्रसादयामास मुनिं नैतदेवं भवेदिति ॥","meaning":{"en":"When these words had been spoken, King Dhritarashtra tried to appease the sage, saying, \"Let it not be so.\""}},{"text":"मैत्रेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Maitreya said:"}},{"n":36,"text":"शमं यास्यति चेत्पुत्रस्तव राजन्यथा तथा ।\nशापो न भविता तात विपरीते भविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"If your son makes peace, king, it will be so and the curse will not take effect; if he does the opposite, it will happen."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":37,"text":"स विलक्षस्तु राजेन्द्र दुर्योधनपिता तदा ।\nमैत्रेयं प्राह किर्मीरः कथं भीमेन पातितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Duryodhana's father, abashed, lord of kings, asked Maitreya, \"How was Kirmira felled by Bhima?\""}},{"text":"मैत्रेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Maitreya said:"}},{"n":38,"text":"नाहं वक्ष्याम्यसूया ते न ते शुश्रूषते सुतः ।\nएष ते विदुरः सर्वमाख्यास्यति गते मयि ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will not tell you, out of displeasure; your son does not wish to hear. Vidura will tell you everything after I have gone."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":39,"text":"इत्येवमुक्त्वा मैत्रेयः प्रातिष्ठत यथागतम् ।\nकिर्मीरवधसंविग्नो बहिर्दुर्योधनोऽगमत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So saying, Maitreya went back as he had come, and Duryodhana, troubled at the killing of Kirmira, went outside."}}]}]}